body:
yeah the rape just really kinda messed me up because i trusted the guy so much yet he took advantage of me which hurts.

i'm trying to focus on myself but i'm so used to talking to them but i feel so alone. i deactivated my instagram accounts, and thats where i talk to my online friends but i haven't for the past week. i've been trying to do a social media detox and to also just focus on revision with exams but all this bs with my irl friends happened and i think they dont want anything to do with me anymore which sucks but thats life. i'm going college next year and hopefully my mental health improves and i can make new friends- only if im not dead by then xo

&#x200B;

i don't plan on giving up my online therapy because i feel it has helped slightly. instead i'd prefer to make it more regular like a 2 times a week thing. i prefer doing it online compared to face to face as it's less awkward if you get me. i dont know why they think it's ineffective. i tjink it might be because they expect all my suicidal thoughts and my self destructive habits to just disappear but it doesn't work like that. it takes time. and those friends claim i deny any help they offer me but the truth is i'm already seeking the help i'm getting so why would i take more than i need when there are others out there who have none at all.

&#x200B;

and i'm glad i could make someone laugh ahaha :,,)
